WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.370
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:45.500
the Kingdom of Chin launched an invasion
of the neighboring land of Gi.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.660
Ou Hon, Mou Ten, and Shin:

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.370
these bold soldiers and aspiring
great generals were together here now,

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.160
ready to usher in a brand-new age!

00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.120
On the recommendation of commanding
general Mou Gou of the Chin army,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.160
Shin was promoted to thousand-man
commander--albeit only temporarily.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.790
At the same time, the legendary
general Ren Pa and his army

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:12.750
were moving out of the Gi capital
and toward the front lines.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:19.660
"The Night Before Battle"

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.620
Man, what a sight, eh, En?
That's a thousand troops--a thousand!

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.910
Yes, well...

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:44.620
S-Shin is totally unflappable,
even starin' down a thousand men!

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.830
Amazing! That's our commander, all right!

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.580
He just doesn't know any better.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:54.370
But can he still talk to us like this?

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:58.790
Check out the new 700 troops!

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.410
Some are on horseback, and even
the infantrymen are all armored...

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.870
They've got to be nobility--
from the warrior class.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.950
Wonder if they're ticked off,
being lumped in with us farmer types.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.750
Probably.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.290
700 former members of Kaku Bi's unit!

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.040
Face Commander Shin...

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.040
...and salute!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.830
K-Kaku Bi's unit?!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.580
Don't let those nobles beat you, Shin!

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:43.750
Kaku Bi had often told us of
the exploits of the Hi Shin Unit.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.620
We are proud to have
been made a part of that unit.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.950
Starting today, we will risk
our lives as the Hi Shin Unit,

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.910
but please allow us to keep
in our hearts as we fight

00:03:55.910 --> 00:04:00.410
our memories of Kaku Bi, cut down too soon.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.370
Of course.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.250
What's your name?

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.790
So Sui, former lieutenant of Kaku Bi's unit.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.250
It is a pleasure to meet you.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:18.830
All right. So Sui,
you'll be a lieutenant here, too.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.700
There's a lotta stuff I'd like you to teach me.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.700
Sir!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:32.580
And we're thrilled to be able
to fight alongside Kaku Bi's men!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.450
But as Lieutenant So Sui said,

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.700
from here on out, we're all one Hi Shin Unit!

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.870
Here, there's no difference
between noble and farmer!

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.700
No difference between old-timer and new recruit!

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:51.580
Bring your burdens--as long as you fight!

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.700
That's how we come together as one huge group...

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.450
...and destroy the enemy!

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.370
Let's do this, Hi Shin Unit!

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.160
We're after the enemy general...

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.500
...and we're takin' Ren Pa's head!

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.410
Fantastic! Shin's amazing!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.330
Yeah! We've got Kaku Bi's unit with us now!

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:20.000
One element of an excellent
general is having a <i>voice</i> .

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.750
A general needs a powerful voice
to convey his words,

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:26.290
to address his troops and raise morale,

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:31.540
and Shin's voice was remarkably effective.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:36.580
All who heard it got a deep sense
of the passion it contained.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.620
It proved to be just what the new
thousand-man Hi Shin Unit needed

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.330
to get off to a good start.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:53.500
Meanwhile, news of General Ren Pa
and his army had reached Kanyou.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.580
Shou Hei Kun,
why won't you send reinforcements?

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.080
They're up against Ren Pa!

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:07.000
We had taken his appearance
into account, as a precaution.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.660
Mou Gou's army has the might to handle him.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:15.580
Besides, we can't afford
reinforcements right now.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:21.450
As a foothold on the way to the center of Chin,

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.160
Sanyou is ripe for the taking.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:28.080
But if we go after Sanyou,
we won't only be fighting Gi--

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.790
Kan and So, to the south,
will make their moves as well.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:38.200
Again, So will want to prevent Chin
from taking Sanyou.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:46.250
Sanyou here is the largest barrier
to expanding Chin's borders.

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.910
It is impossible.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:53.620
According to the reports,
Mou Gou has 140 thousand men--

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.660
as does Ren Pa's Gi army.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.580
They cannot defeat Ren Pa
with an equal number of troops.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:04.080
Our military's high commander
does not know how fearsome Ren Pa is.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.040
While fully aware it presents some difficulties,

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.910
we must act now, while we are allied with Sho.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.040
Whatever happens,

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.950
we must take Sanyou in this battle--

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:24.200
that is, if Chin is serious about
a unified Middle Kingdom!

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:44.040
My lord,

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.040
what was that look in the King's eyes?

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:54.120
That look meant that he knows everything.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.620
He knows everything, and yet dares say nothing.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.370
Those eyes

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.330
aren't looking at me and the Queen Dowager.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.330
Honestly...

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:08.330
Sir?

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.830
Yes, that's what I'm after:
a unified Middle Kingdom.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.870
I cannot stop until I reach it,

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:26.700
whether I face a minister or one
of the world's greatest generals!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.200
Shin...

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.120
I'm the one who made a promise.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.290
And <i>I'm</i> not about to lose, either, Shin!

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:51.160
The struggles within the
Royal Court died down that day.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.080
Though only for a moment,

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:57.660
the Kingdom of Chin came together
as one in the capture of Sanyou.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.120
Hey there,

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.700
thousand-man commander Mou Ten!

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:08.040
Well, hello yourself,
thousand-man commander Shin!

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.700
The Hi Shin Unit has
Kaku Bi's troops now, right?

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.540
Yeah, actually.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.540
No fair! Those're some heavy hitters!

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:19.750
It's totally fair!

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:25.330
I'd say your first meeting
with the troops went well, then.

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.500
You bet! How about you?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.160
Easy-peasy.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.830
I mean, I'm Little Lord Commander here.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.540
I don't even have to say anything,
and they all bow their heads.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:43.200
That's right--he's Mou Bu's son
and General Mou Gou's grandson.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.620
Not that I see the resemblance...

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:49.080
It may only be temporary, but we're
definitely thousand-man commanders

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.040
in this battle, anyway.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:54.040
Feels like you're
rubbing shoulders with generals

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.580
when you've got a thousand men
under you, y'know?

00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.370
Yeah...

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.950
Sure does.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.790
Hey, thousand-man commander Shin!

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.790
Hey, thousand-man commander Mou Ten!

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.120
What the hell are they doing?

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.200
You two are far too giddy.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.290
Well, well!

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:22.950
If it isn't thousand-man commander Ou Hon!

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.370
Hey, thousand-man commander Ou Hon!

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.540
Shut up.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.790
You don't understand the position you're in.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.950
As General Mou Gou said,
there are plenty of troops here

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:40.660
who are jealous of our promotions.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:45.660
Well, it's not good news for anyone
looking to climb the ol' ladder,

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.950
us being so young and all.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.250
Ha! That has nothin' to do with it!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:54.290
Problem is, those jealous types
are in the upper ranks as well.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:00.790
If we lose this battle, we'll
likely be treated as war criminals.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.750
I suppose we will.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:08.870
So stop joking around
and start thinking tactics.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:13.540
A thousand-man unit is big enough
to turn the tide of battle.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.750
Big enough to turn the tide of battle...!

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.500
Ugh! Get a load of Mr. High-and-Mighty!

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.580
Why's he always gotta be so uptight? The jerk!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:32.830
Don't be that way.
Being a noble is a big responsibility.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:37.660
If it's <i>too</i> big, you wind up
an irresponsible fellow like me,

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:41.200
or a stern, rugged guy like him.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.950
Especially when your father is larger than life.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:45.950
Huh?

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:53.580
Flanked by two lieutenants' armies,
the reshuffled Mou Gou army

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:57.700
approached their final destination: Sanyou.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:04.290
Meanwhile, in the castle of kankan
in Gi's neighboring land of Sho...

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:08.910
An urgent message!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.790
San Pi Jo Castle has fallen
to the Chin army's lieutenant!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.000
What?!

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.620
So soon?

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.700
How many <i>is</i> that?!

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:24.660
Mou Gou's army has taken three,
these lieutenants have taken five, and...

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:27.660
now the other lieutenant
has taken castle number eight.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.290
Eight?!

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.250
In such a short time?

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:34.370
Mou Gou's army is as strong as I'd expected...

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:39.910
but his lieutenants are stronger than I'd hoped.

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:44.250
How did I overlook them so completely?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:45.790
Who <i>are</i> these two?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:53.000
"Ou Hon"

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.870
L-Ri Boku, sir...

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.580
This isn't good.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:04.410
If Chin manages to take Sanyou,

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:09.290
they'll gain a major foothold
into the Middle Kingdom's interior.

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:16.660
We should be sending reinforcements
to Gi to help put a stop to this,

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:20.330
but we can't--not with this alliance in the way.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:26.290
So Shou Hei Kun's the one who put
together this assault on Sanyou.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:31.160
It's a bold move, one he can only make now.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:35.500
Urgent! General Ren Pa
has passed Sanyou Castle!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.500
Passed it?! He didn't go inside?

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.120
So it's a field battle!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:44.370
Amazing... It's just as Ri Boku predicted.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:48.080
General Ren Pa does seem confident.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:53.700
Let us watch the battle develop
and pray he is victorious.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.290
Will that be enough?

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:58.700
In all likelihood, the Gi army will win.

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:04.540
In any case, there's no general
alive on this earth

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:08.950
who could defeat him face to face--me included.

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:14.370
It had been about two months
since the Chin army had begun

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.330
its invasion of Gi.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.870
At long last, Ren Pa had arrived at Sanyou,

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:21.910
where the decisive battle would be held.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:26.000
But the reason Ren Pa hadn't positioned himself

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.330
in the more advantageous mountains...

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:36.250
...was because the Chin army's
lieutenant was already there.

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:42.540
I give them full marks for that, I suppose.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.450
Tiger--a tiger!

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.250
Shin, look! You said you
wanted to see a tiger, right?

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.580
Quiet!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:58.750
What are you, nuts?
Don't you be interrupting Shin!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.290
Those four are busy...

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:04.120
coming up with strategies
for the thousand-man Hi Shin Unit.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:10.160
Now move the third squadron two to the right.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.370
Chu Tetsu! Two squares right!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:16.750
That's left. Two to <i>our</i> right!

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:18.700
Not three squares--two!

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:21.120
No, that's <i>left</i> , I said!

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.950
Then when the first squadron
circles around, we'll win.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:26.160
Maybe.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:31.080
Wh-Where on earth did you
study tactics, Kyou Kai?

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:37.540
Study? I didn't.
It's just something I thought up. That's all.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.580
A-Are you some kind of genius...?

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.000
Yep, Kyou Kai really is somethin'!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.120
But you should see him with his sword out! Yow!

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:50.290
I'm tellin' ya, you'll be damn glad
you're on the same side!

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:54.660
Well, anyway, this looks good.

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:57.250
Let's see what other strategies
we can come up with.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:58.250
Sir!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:03.000
Ren Pa, sir!

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:07.200
A Chin army lieutenant has arrived at Ryu Zan!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.620
They seem to be taking their position there!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:10.620
On Ryu Zan?!

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:13.950
Whatever for? That mountain is
a good distance from what should be

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.830
the main battlefield.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:18.200
Have they gotten the place wrong?

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:20.450
Or perhaps they have cold feet!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:25.910
Hmph. If that was on purpose,
that's one quirky general.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:29.910
Strategists who favor change
often look to keep a distance.

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:34.870
Sounds just like a certain
ever-changing old man I know!

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:41.410
And what's going on
with Mou Gou's main army?

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:46.080
They're in the countryside.
We expect them to arrive tomorrow.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.410
Our troops should all
be in place tomorrow as well.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:52.870
Then the battle begins tomorrow!

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:55.700
Bring liquor!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:17:00.000
We celebrate our impending victory!
Every soldier gets a drink!

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.700
Tomorrow, huh...

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:19.330
Ready... go!

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.120
Hey! Don't be hittin' with your head like that!

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.000
I'll show you!

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.330
Ha! Look who's talking!

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:31.330
Oh, yeah?

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.040
Whoa! You both lost!

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:36.040
Say <i>what</i> ?!

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:39.330
Whatta buncha dolts!

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:51.200
Ready...

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.200
...go!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:55.870
Go, Ryuu Sen!

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.910
All right, Ryuu Sen--let's do this!

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:01.000
Huh? B-But...

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.450
Go on, Ryuu Sen!
It doesn't matter if he's the commander!

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:06.370
Just don't get hurt, bossman!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.120
There's...

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:12.700
There's too big a gap in strength between us...

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.870
Wh-What should I do?

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:17.870
If I just up and beat him...

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:19.620
Go!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:20.870
What was <i>that</i> , Shin?

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.540
Some commander you are! That was pitiful!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:25.500
Useless! Moron! Dummy!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.120
That's our Ryuu Sen!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.540
Maybe <i>he</i> should be our commander!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.870
Yeah!

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.370
Commander Ryuu Sen!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:37.200
Commander Ryuu Sen! Commander Ryuu Sen!

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:38.750
I could live with that.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:40.830
Okay, here goes. Ready...

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:47.910
Hyou told me once:
These contests ain't about brute strength.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:50.040
There's a trick to 'em.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:55.250
First, as you clasp hands, try to
look weak--but don't get found out.

00:18:55.250 --> 00:18:56.830
The second it begins,

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.330
use all your joints

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:03.250
to move the strength from
all your muscles into your right arm...

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:04.700
...and make it explode!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.700
Go!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.290
Yesss!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.040
Whoa! That was insane, Shin!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.700
I knew you could do it!

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.750
Commander Shin!

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.950
--Commander Shin! Commander Shin!
--How'd ya like <i>that</i> ?

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.580
Commander Shin!

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:28.450
What's up, Kyou Kai?

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:31.790
Shin... Do you have a moment?

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.290
We need to talk.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:49.620
I don't have my feet on the ground.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.410
That's why I'm not moving
forward like the rest of you.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:01.910
And that's because I haven't
avenged my sister Kou.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:11.200
I still clearly remember
the pain of that moment.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.950
And yet,

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:21.370
I put my revenge aside, and I wound up here.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:25.200
I'm certain that's because...

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.500
...this...

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:32.790
This is the only home
I have to go back to now.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:36.700
Shin,

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:43.580
it's like you said:
There's more to life after revenge.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.660
Otherwise,

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:48.660
how can Kou rest easy,
with her dreams of the wide world?

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:56.040
And I... I share her dreams.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:08.410
But that road lies beyond my avenging Kou.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.500
And that's why...

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:18.660
That's why I'm leaving when this battle is over.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:22.910
I don't know how many months,
how many years it will take,

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:24.660
but I <i>will</i> have my revenge.

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:31.290
And once I have, when I come back here,

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:40.120
I think I should be able
to move forward with all of you.

00:21:43.620 --> 00:21:44.910
Fine by me!

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:52.540
Actually, I was just thinkin'
you oughta be doin' somethin' like that.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.040
When you said we needed to talk,

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:57.200
I was terrified you were leavin' right away!

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.200
Not till my job is done.

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:03.620
So this battle'll be your parting gift...

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:07.830
Let's win it, Kyou Kai.

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:14.830
Yeah.

00:22:17.950 --> 00:22:22.660
Y'know, you <i>are</i> pretty cute.
'Specially when you smile.

00:22:22.660 --> 00:22:23.660
What?

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:36.250
A message from General Do Mon to all troops!

00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:43.910
The Gi army's First Brigade
and the Chin army's lieutenants

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:46.540
have arrived at Sanyou, our final destination!

00:22:46.540 --> 00:22:51.000
Both armies are in a standoff
as they await their allies' arrival!

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.700
The Gi army is gathering as we speak!

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:56.660
We can't let them get the jump on us!

00:22:56.660 --> 00:23:02.330
Now we march--all of us!
The deciding battle is nigh!

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:04.040
Forward!

00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:10.580
Now <i>this</i> is more like it!

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:11.580
Yes.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:15.660
All right!

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:18.040
Let's go, Hi Shin Unit!

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.050
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"Charge!"
